; getquad_index_out_of_range: a quadratic read past the extent must raise.
;
; Both VMs used to answer 0 here, so this is the one vector in the group that
; pins a decision rather than closing a divergence. A GETQUAD that reads back
; 0 from a pair SETQUAD refuses would leave one instruction family
; disagreeing with itself about which variables exist, so the read is bounded
; like the write. spec/xqvm/ISA.md's coefficient-access precondition states
; it for the whole section.
;
; The pair is asymmetric and only j is out of range, so a check written
; against i alone fails here rather than passing by symmetry.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0

PUSH 1           ; i, in range
PUSH 9           ; j, past the extent
GETQUAD r0
HALT
